          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "text": "A patient’s own blood stem cells have just been collected by apheresis, ready to be frozen and given back after high-dose chemotherapy."
        },
        {
          "id": "h2",
          "start": 7,
          "end": 14,
          "text": "Before freezing, the lab must answer one question: are there enough stem cells in this bag for the marrow to recover?"
        },
        {
          "id": "h3",
          "start": 14,
          "end": 20,
          "text": "The answer is a number: CD34-positive cells per kilogram of the patient’s body weight."
